          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: la alegría",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "la alegría — \"joy, happiness\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Tu visita es una alegría. Your visit is a joy."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "¡Qué alegría! — How lovely! It is built on alegre, cheerful."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "alegría is built on alegre \"cheerful\", which is usually traced to Latin alacer \"lively, brisk\" through a spoken form alecrem; English alacrity comes from the same Latin word."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
