              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "la dicha — \"happiness, good fortune\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "¡Qué dicha verte otra vez! What joy to see you again!"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "More literary than la alegría. Nunca es tarde si la dicha es buena — better late than never."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "dicha is inherited from Latin dicta \"things said\" (EtymDB), from dīcere \"to say\"; the usual reading is that good fortune was what fate had said for you."
            }
          ]
        },
